From d79543687c120230584eb5a03d30565e2e6ebd0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ci <ci@local>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 05:57:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: fsl: qbman: add CEETM hierarchical egress shaper support

Port the QorIQ QMan CEETM (Customer Edge Egress Traffic Management) API
from the legacy NXP SDK, modernised to mainline style. Provides
hierarchical dual-rate shaping (LNI + channel), strict-priority class
scheduling and byte/frame tail-drop congestion groups on the FMan egress
path of DPAA1 SoCs, hard-coded for the LS1046A CEETM0 instance (DCP0).

New optional symbol FSL_QMAN_CEETM (default n) builds qman_ceetm.c. CEETM
management commands (verbs 0x70-0x7D) ride the existing affine-portal MC
ring through one generic helper, qman_ceetm_mc_exec(), added to qman.c.
The SDK bitfield wire structs are reimplemented with explicit __beN
fields and big-endian byte arrays. CCSR additions (prescaler, sub-portal
CEETM-mode enable/disable, qman_clk from DT clock-frequency) live in
qman_ccsr.c.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
